        {
            "label": "Creator of",
            "name": "Vyzora",
            "slug": "vyzora",
            "tagline": "Analytics that respect user privacy.",
            "description": "Vyzora is a privacy-first, horizontally scalable analytics platform for real-time event tracking without invasive data collection.",
            "longDescription": "Vyzora is a privacy-first analytics platform engineered from the ground up to give developers deep product insights without compromising their users' data. In an era where third-party analytics tools phone home, fingerprint users, and sell behavioral data — Vyzora keeps everything self-hosted and under your control.\n\nDevelopers integrate a tiny client-side JavaScript snippet (under 4KB gzipped) that tracks page views, custom events, and user sessions — all anonymized via server-side hashing, with no cookies or persistent identifiers stored on the client.\n\nThe backend is built for horizontal scalability: events flow through a message queue before being written to the database in batches, ensuring the ingestion layer can absorb traffic spikes without affecting dashboard query performance. The real-time dashboard uses WebSocket subscriptions to show live visitor counts, popular pages, and event funnels.",
            "highlights": [
                "Zero third-party dependencies — 100% self-hosted and GDPR-friendly",
                "Client snippet under 4KB gzipped — negligible page load impact",
                "Session reconstruction without cookies or persistent client identifiers",
                "Real-time dashboard via WebSocket subscriptions",
                "Horizontal scalability with message-queue-backed ingestion pipeline",
                "Aggregated metric visualizations: funnels, heatmaps, retention curves",
                "REST API for embedding analytics data in external dashboards"
            ],
