        {
            "label": "Creator of",
            "name": "Learning's Hub",
            "slug": "learnings-hub",
            "tagline": "Master DSA, and Development Skills with Proper Tracking.",
            "description": "Learning's Hub helps developers track DSA and programming progress with custom lists, public sharing, and community-based learning.",
            "longDescription": "Learning's Hub is a full-stack web application that solves one of the most overlooked problems in developer growth: tracking what you've actually learned versus what you've just skimmed. Most developers jump between YouTube, LeetCode, and documentation tabs with no unified record of their progress.\n\nWith Learning's Hub, you build structured learning lists — whether that's 'Blind 75 LeetCode problems', 'JavaScript Fundamentals', or a custom roadmap — and track your completion status, notes, and revisit flags per item. Lists can be kept private or shared publicly with a unique link, enabling community-based accountability.\n\nThe platform supports community discovery: you can browse other users' public lists, fork them to your account, and adapt them. A gamified progress system shows streaks, completion percentages, and weekly goals — keeping motivation high through data-driven feedback.",
            "highlights": [
                "Structured learning lists for DSA, languages, and custom roadmaps",
                "Per-item completion tracking with personal notes and revisit flags",
                "Public list sharing with unique shareable links",
                "Community discovery — browse, fork, and adapt other users' lists",
                "Gamified progress: streaks, completion %, weekly goals",
                "Supports 50+ built-in DSA problem sets mapped to LeetCode",
                "Full authentication with JWT — plans are persisted per user"
            ],
